"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,928\nThe Learning Brain\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,235\nEpisode 1\n\n3\n00:00:07,315 --> 00:00:09,309\nNeuroplasticity\n\n4\n00:00:12,109 --> 00:00:13,834\nYour brain is not finished.\n\n5\n00:00:14,215 --> 00:00:16,023\nEvery time you learn something,\n\n6\n00:00:16,043 --> 00:00:17,476\nit physically changes.\n\n7\n00:00:17,811 --> 00:00:22,612\nThat is neuroplasticity, and it is the foundation for everything in this series.\n\n8\n00:00:22,782 --> 00:00:24,740\nLearning happens at synapses,\n\n9\n00:00:24,944 --> 00:00:28,733\nthe tiny gaps where one neuron passes a signal to the next.\n\n10\n00:00:29,165 --> 00:00:31,164\nUse a connection again and again,\n\n11\n00:00:31,341 --> 00:00:34,066\nand the receiving cell becomes more responsive.\n\n12\n00:00:34,625 --> 00:00:36,931\nSame message, bigger response.\n\n13\n00:00:37,182 --> 00:00:39,838\nThat is called long term potentiation.\n\n14\n00:00:40,008 --> 00:00:44,233\nKeep practicing, and neurons grow new branches and new contacts.\n\n15\n00:00:44,579 --> 00:00:46,287\nCells that fire together,\n\n16\n00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:47,403\nwire together.\n\n17\n00:00:47,872 --> 00:00:50,615\nWell used pathways get wrapped in myelin,\n\n18\n00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:53,264\nan insulation that speeds signals up.\n\n19\n00:00:53,701 --> 00:00:55,825\nAnd connections you stop using weaken,\n\n20\n00:00:55,845 --> 00:00:57,145\nand get pruned away.\n\n21\n00:00:57,315 --> 00:00:59,544\nYou can see this in brain scans.\n\n22\n00:00:59,846 --> 00:01:01,631\nIn a 2004 study,\n\n23\n00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:04,672\ntwelve adults spent three months learning to juggle.\n\n24\n00:01:05,163 --> 00:01:09,118\nGrey matter grew in an area that processes visual motion.\n\n25\n00:01:09,536 --> 00:01:11,787\nThree months after they stopped practicing,\n\n26\n00:01:11,999 --> 00:01:13,768\nmuch of that growth had faded.\n\n27\n00:01:13,938 --> 00:01:19,300\nLondon taxi drivers spend three to four years learning about twenty five thousand streets.\n\n28\n00:01:19,676 --> 00:01:23,337\nResearchers scanned seventy nine trainees before and after.\n\n29\n00:01:23,889 --> 00:01:28,495\nThe thirty nine who qualified gained grey matter at the back of the hippocampus,\n\n30\n00:01:28,711 --> 00:01:30,103\na key memory region.\n\n31\n00:01:30,581 --> 00:01:33,960\nThose who failed, and a control group,\n\n32\n00:01:33,972 --> 00:01:34,265\nshowed no change.\n\n33\n00:01:34,435 --> 00:01:35,409\nSome caution.\n\n34\n00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:37,255\nThese are small studies,\n\n35\n00:01:37,275 --> 00:01:38,914\nand scans measure volume,\n\n36\n00:01:38,934 --> 00:01:40,372\nnot exactly what grew.\n\n37\n00:01:40,838 --> 00:01:42,658\nBigger is not always better.\n\n38\n00:01:42,951 --> 00:01:45,185\nAnd these changes take weeks to years,\n\n39\n00:01:45,205 --> 00:01:46,061\nnot minutes.\n\n40\n00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,001\nFor teaching.\n\n41\n00:01:47,379 --> 00:01:49,162\nPlan for repeated practice,\n\n42\n00:01:49,258 --> 00:01:50,860\nnot a single exposure.\n\n43\n00:01:51,206 --> 00:01:54,473\nSpace it out, so the same pathways are used again.\n\n44\n00:01:54,896 --> 00:01:56,520\nMake students do the thinking,\n\n45\n00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:59,675\nbecause the brain changes in response to what it does.\n\n46\n00:01:59,978 --> 00:02:02,118\nAnd come back to old material,\n\n47\n00:02:02,138 --> 00:02:03,171\nor it fades.\n\n48\n00:02:03,341 --> 00:02:05,468\nPractice is not just repetition.\n\n49\n00:02:05,771 --> 00:02:06,943\nIt is construction.\n\n50\n00:02:07,170 --> 00:02:09,809\nAnd neural plasticity never switches off.\n\n"
